{"step_index":1344,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:59:55Z","thinking":"**Investigating CORS Behavior Discrepancy**\n\nThe HTTP/2 200 response reveals the correct `access-control-allow-origin` header is already present, alongside `access-control-allow-methods: GET` and `access-control-allow-credentials: true`, indicating the Spring Boot Actuator supports CORS natively for GET and OPTIONS requests. The manual addition of `add_header Access-Control-Allow-Origin '*'` in Nginx resulted in a different response, suggesting a conflict or overriding behavior. This warrants investigation into Nginx's configuration and whether it's interfering with the pre-existing CORS settings from the application.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Document CORS duplicate resolution and native Tomcat CORS\"","EndLine":"145","Instruction":"\"Update remediation section with discovery of duplicate CORS and removal of manual Nginx add_header\"","ReplacementContent":"\"### B. Dual CORS Header Conflict\\n* **Discovery**: Spring Boot Actuator on Tomcat **natively** provides CORS support and dynamically reflects the exact client origin (e.g. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://centreonpro.intranet.local` with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`).\\n* **The Conflict**: Adding `add_header Access-Control-Allow-Origin '*'` in Nginx caused **duplicate** CORS headers to be returned to the browser:\\n  1. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://centreonpro.intranet.local` (from Tomcat)\\n  2. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` (from Nginx)\\n* **The Browser Block**: Per the W3C / Fetch CORS specification, a response MUST NOT contain multiple `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` headers, and wildcard `*` is strictly forbidden when `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` is present. Modern browsers (Firefox / Chrome) automatically reject the response as a CORS violation.\\n* **The Resolution**: Removed the manual CORS `add_header` block in Nginx to allow Tomcat's native, dynamic CORS to pass through cleanly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Applied on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`\\n\\nThe configuration [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) has been finalized:\\n\\n1. **Clean Header Proxification**:\\n   * Removed `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` include to eliminate duplicate `Host:` injection.\\n   * Defined clean, RFC-compliant singular proxy headers.\\n   * Allowed Tomcat to manage CORS dynamically without conflicting header injection.\\n\\n2. **Validation & Reload**:\\n   * `nginx -t`: **Syntax OK, test successful**.\\n   * Recharged seamlessly via `systemctl reload nginx`.\"","StartLine":"70","TargetContent":"\"### B. Missing CORS Headers (Browser AJAX Block)\\n* In [`listOptions.js`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266):\\n  ```javascript\\n  function testServerAddressNg() {\\n    const urlServerNg = jQuery('input[name=\\\"server_address_ng\\\"]').val();\\n    jQuery.ajax({\\n      type : 'GET',\\n      url : `${urlServerNg}/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health`\\n    });\\n  }\\n  ```\\n* The test button is triggered directly by the **client web browser** from origin `https://extranetclient...` (port 443) targeting port 9443.\\n* Modern browsers strictly block cross-origin requests unless the target server returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Applied on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`\\n\\nThe configuration [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) has been upgraded:\\n\\n1. **Clean Header Proxification**:\\n   * Removed `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` include to eliminate all duplicate header injection.\\n   * Defined clean, RFC-compliant singular proxy headers:\\n     ```nginx\\n     proxy_set_header Host              $http_host;\\n     proxy_set_header X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;\\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Ssl   on;\\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host  $host;\\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port  9443;\\n     ```\\n\\n2. **Full CORS Support Added**:\\n   ```nginx\\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*' always;\\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS, PUT, DELETE' always;\\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type,Range,Authorization' always;\\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Expose-Headers' 'Content-Length,Content-Range' always;\\n\\n   if ($request_method = 'OPTIONS') {\\n       add_header 'Access-Control-A\n<truncated 601 bytes>","TargetFile":"\"/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md\"","toolAction":"\"Updating report\"","toolSummary":"\"Update report with CORS fix\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
