{"step_index":1348,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:04:30Z","content":"**SKADOOSH! That is what I am talking about!** \n\nBoth checkmarks <span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">GREEN</span> and the Map interface fully loaded and rendering cleanly! \n\n---\n\n### Quick Recap of What We Conquered:\n\n1. **Passwordless DNS-01 Let's Encrypt Issuance**: Automated DNS challenge injection directly into PowerDNS Master (`th2-dnsp-mst1`) via `id_ed25519` key without APIs or passwords.\n2. **Dedicated Nginx Vhost (`03-map...`)**: Decoupled port `9443` into a dedicated, clean configuration listening on both internal DMZ and public VIP with its own independent access/error logs.\n3. **Tomcat RFC 7230 Compliance**: Eradicated the duplicate `Host:` header that was triggering Tomcat's strict `400 Bad Request`.\n4. **Clean Native CORS Handshake**: Eliminated double-origin header conflicts so Firefox and Chromium accept the actuator telemetry and map streams natively with credentials.\n5. **Internal Proxy Bypass**: Configured workstation `no_proxy` and GNOME exceptions so office workstations talk directly to the reverse proxy while leaving your Squid proxy and `apt update` 100% operational.\n\nDon't forget to click **Save** at the bottom of the **Administration > Extensions > Options** page so Centreon persists those URLs in the database!\n\nEverything is documented and archived in your report artifact:  \n[centreon-map-chain-report.md](file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md).\n\nEnjoy your fully operational Centreon Map!","thinking":"**Celebrating Successful Infrastructure Deployment**\n\nExcellent! The user confirms a green test result and proper map UI loading. The Let's Encrypt production issuance is now verified. Another victory for flawless execution!\n\n\n"}
