t vars. Vault password: \"koby\".\n14: - Bash sandbox blocks outbound SSH to non-whitelisted hosts; user had to run the ansible-playbook command themselves via `!` prefix (auto-mode classifier blocks `dangerouslyDisableSandbox` for this even from me).\n15: - Ran into a separate local bug: `ansible-playbook` errors with \"requires blocking IO on stdin/stdout/stderr\" in this shell — worked around with `script -qec \"...\" /dev/null` to allocate a pty.\n16: - 172.30.249.209 has no inventory entry (ad hoc `-i \"172.30.249.209,\"` used); not documented anywhere else — its OS/purpose is unknown to me.\n17: \n18: ## Automated SSH & KeePass Integration\n19: - Tool: `/home/koby/.local/bin/kssh` (symlinked from `~/.ansible/scripts/kssh.py`).\n20: - Whenever user asks to SSH to a server, automatically run `kssh <server>` or query `~/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json` via `build_kdbx_pool.py`.\n21: - Auto-extracts IP, port (e.g. 30), user, key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`), and password.\n22: - Attempts passwordless key (`koby-bowser-ansible` or target user) first; falls back to `sshpass` using the database password.\n23: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
